cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sdrmesh: software-defined BLE and LoRa physical layers for the meshfind mesh"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
authors:
  - name: "the sdrmesh authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/coopersimpson101-debug/sdrmesh"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  BLE LE 1M (GFSK) and LoRa (chirp spread spectrum) physical layers written from scratch in Python/NumPy:
  modulators, channel selection, CFO/STO estimation, Gardner timing recovery, sync-word correlation,
  de-whitening, CRC-24, LoRa Gray mapping, diagonal interleaving, Hamming FEC, header and CRC, with an
  AWGN/CFO/timing/multipath channel model, Monte Carlo BER/PER against theory, SigMF/HackRF/PlutoSDR I/O and a
  streaming receiver that decodes meshfind tag adverts.
keywords:
  - software-defined radio
  - Bluetooth Low Energy
  - LoRa
  - GFSK
  - chirp spread spectrum
  - digital signal processing
  - HackRF
  - PlutoSDR
